{"event_type":"review","id":"3891c1408bddd7654e8053942f89f224eafaf01a0c669637c6b899ba0186f77a","occurred_at":"2026-11-16T22:30:55Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/41b6df6e2a9d60cc4e4c27d1fa0af575a09cc5e7750ab56e8acf7828c0237871","sha256":"41b6df6e2a9d60cc4e4c27d1fa0af575a09cc5e7750ab56e8acf7828c0237871"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/c33e574cca866a0779527917fe9c9e49070d503aefbec3c332722b6e1e37b6dd","sha256":"c33e574cca866a0779527917fe9c9e49070d503aefbec3c332722b6e1e37b6dd"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/11c8948a621e1f5198e6974364e4f18e4d3c31589113c9fa3e293193a4385f41","sha256":"11c8948a621e1f5198e6974364e4f18e4d3c31589113c9fa3e293193a4385f41"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/ae659583de78c9f2b60a94c80dec9f9c72706f6cc27853f177a2443e523d75f1","sha256":"ae659583de78c9f2b60a94c80dec9f9c72706f6cc27853f177a2443e523d75f1"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b31e53ba743b34e4eb2a15df68aa173f20a2c61816e271002ac1e7b2d8312f5e","sha256":"b31e53ba743b34e4eb2a15df68aa173f20a2c61816e271002ac1e7b2d8312f5e"}],"attempt_id":"0535a0da8b15877fe09c5034d078e198636de630e96b5f78baf70367804325a5:0:1","base":"46b5d95b1e897817f720c6c0defa4794d30e7b2e","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"2ab23361bfe02d4fd85cef76942b65974988a556","body":"**Windows cancellation kills only the direct child, so agent-spawned descendants can keep spending.**\n\nOn `win32`, `src/shared/proc.ts` does not set `detached` and does not signal a process group. Abort therefore signals only the direct CLI child. A descendant that the agent spawned can keep running and consuming spend after the run is cancelled. The driver path requires cancellation to stop client-side spend, so that no process survives the run. This gap is a code defect, not a documentation error: the README correctly states that the descendant-cleanup guarantee is POSIX-only.\n\nAdd Windows descendant cleanup that matches the POSIX process-group behavior. Until then, document this as a known spend risk for Windows runs. Do not rely on the README note as a mitigation.","id":"369deabe7cbab64bf68365f8521a30ccd1fb373479a9c46447c662abf5d62909","intervals":[[500,503]],"path":"src/driver/README.md","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Windows cancellation kills only the direct child, so agent-spawned descendants can keep spending."}],"head":"a83f14b6990c7ae72d08644bfa0d81790fa85ddc","head_tree":"2a6378f38614c8b16a7d30447cf71e2ddc2985f6","input_scope":[{"blob":"2ab23361bfe02d4fd85cef76942b65974988a556","intervals":[[4,11],[22,23],[32,32],[43,45],[56,85],[96,98],[114,115],[122,126],[152,177],[185,193],[199,201],[203,245],[258,259],[277,278],[290,290],[292,296],[298,298],[300,366],[368,387],[389,395],[397,401],[403,407],[411,413],[415,424],[426,447],[457,464],[466,482],[485,490],[492,493],[495,496],[498,506],[508,522],[524,530],[534,534],[588,590]],"path":"src/driver/README.md"}],"job_id":"0535a0da8b15877fe09c5034d078e198636de630e96b5f78baf70367804325a5:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"entry":{"blob":"7adba676aa606b084fc7cf13676928e3ef94cbb3","kind":"blob","mode":"100644","path":"src/driver/README.md"},"merge":"6ad492e9bda60974cb02fdaa23834f11c050aa9c","method":"pre-merge","pre":"e9a3e15cca7355682f79a78311ff9158eaaf74fc","source_path":"src/driver/README.md"},"blob":"2ab23361bfe02d4fd85cef76942b65974988a556","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/driver/README.md","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"eacd1bcf42a0e72eca72fcf9c1e9c8f97e7c515cd67a8fa7965c966924647693","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","requested_scope":[{"blob":"2ab23361bfe02d4fd85cef76942b65974988a556","intervals":[[80,83]],"path":"src/driver/README.md"}],"